hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15517","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Umarah ibn Hadid al-Bajali, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Allah, bless my Ummah in their early mornings, he said: So when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out a detachment, he sent it at the beginning of the day, and Sakhr was a merchant man, and he would not send out his servants except from the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased until he did not know where to place his wealth."
"15522","Hushaym narrated to us: Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Hadid, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my Ummah in their early mornings, he said: So when he sent out a detachment or an army, he sent them from the beginning of the day, he said: And Sakhr was a merchant man, and he used to send out his trade from the beginning of the day, he said: So he became wealthy and his wealth increased."
